map_revelation.text:
You stand at the desk.

{knows_verek_fate?Verek is in the southwest corner. Three hundred and forty people, the last census. The roads leading to it stop because someone drew them stopping. You can see the shape of that decision clearly now.|The southwest corner of the map. The roads that trail off into the valley never struck you as strange before. They do now.}

{saw_margin?The marginal notes are no longer cryptic. They are a record — a specific decision, a specific year, a specific person who is forty feet from where you are standing.|The marginal notes are still unread. You wonder what they say.}

The map is beautiful.{pause}It has not stopped being beautiful.
